    "result_text": "The full suite consists of that single acceptance test (the only test class in the project), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit so that creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges, following the existing per-city-limit pattern in the codebase:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerLimitException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending `LocalDate`, mirroring `CityOwnerLimitException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100` constant and a `requireDailyCapacity()` guard invoked at the start of `addOwner` (before save). It counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count is \u2265 100. Added the needed `LocalDate` and exception imports.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DailyOwnerLimitException` returning `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) with a `ProblemDetail` body, consistent with the other owner-rule handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100 today, 101st rejected) and the full build both pass.\n\nNote: these are code changes in a non-git working directory, so there's nothing to commit unless you'd like me to initialize a repo.",
