        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing structure of this controller:\n\n- `requireDailyCapacity()` is a direct structural sibling of the already-present `requireCityHasCapacity(...)` \u2014 same `findAllOwners().stream().filter(...).count()` shape, same \"counted before save\" doc convention, and it's invoked right next to it in `addOwner`. A maintainer would find this immediately natural.\n- `DailyOwnerLimitException` mirrors `CityOwnerLimitException`, lives in the same `rest.advice` package, and carries just the domain value (`LocalDate`) needed by the advice \u2014 appropriately minimal, not a catch-all.\n- The handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` follows the established per-exception `@ExceptionHandler` + `detailBuild(...)` + `setProperty(\"errors\", ...)` idiom already used throughout that class, returning 429 as specified.\n\nLogic is in the right unit (capacity guard on the controller alongside the other guards), nothing is duplicated beyond the repeated `findAllOwners()` scan that is the pre-existing convention of this class (also used by `countNamesakes` and `generateCustomerCode`), so matching it is the consistent choice rather than a new smell to introduce a one-off abstraction for. No structural improvements warranted."
